/ A json value is item's, not text's (ruling 2, decisions 773 + 774 + 787). A json value
/ can hold any value (a number, a bool, a list, a dict), so its parent is item, not text:
/ Type={item, kind: json} lands as an item whose kind navigates as the "json" type. The
/ asserts are ordered by state: first, while %x% is unread, type.name is "item" and the
/ kind navigates as "json"; then `%x% is text` reads x — the parsed json is a plang dict
/ — so after the read %x% is text is false and type.name narrows to "dict". A value's
/ type is what it is now, and its history is where it came from (787).
JsonIsItemsKind
- variable.set(Name=%x%, Value="{\"a\":1}", Type={name:"item", kind:"json"})
- assert.equals(Expected="item", Actual=%x!type.name%, Message="before any read, x's type name is item")
- assert.equals(Expected="json", Actual=%x!type.kind.name%, Message="before any read, x's kind is the json type")
- condition.if(Left=%x%, Operator="is", Right="text") { variable.set(Name=%isText%, Value=true) }
- assert.equals(Expected=null, Actual=%isText%, Message="x is not a text")
- assert.equals(Expected="dict", Actual=%x!type.name%, Message="after the read, x narrows to a dict")
